  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nSurface low will quickly move east of the area with an initial upper\nimpulse. The next disturbance is quickly following and will pivot \nthrough shortly after daybreak. Once this occurs, the initial shower \nactivity will move out proving a lull. \n\nBut there will be renewed shower development this afternoon with\ninsolation and forcing from the next incoming trough. Showers will\ncontinue well into the evening, perhaps continuing through the\novernight in central Ohio as the upper system slows and gets\nabsorbed into a closed low over eastern Ohio/western Pennsylvania.\n\nProximity of the upper system along with continued northerly low\nlevel flow will keep the potential of some spotty showers into Friday\nand Friday night. Any precipitation should be rather light, but there\nis the possibility that some places could see the first snow flakes\nof the season.",
